{"id": "00000d22-0000-4000-8000-000000000d22", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your RDS instances and Aurora clusters, covering backup settings and best-practice configuration. The scan reads configuration across several accounts and regions, so I'm running it in the background and will summarize what it finds.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_0r5L3d7lTGeR3U7OKz07p8", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "rds-aurora-review", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review all Amazon RDS DB instances and Aurora DB clusters for best-practices compliance and backup configuration. READ-ONLY only (describe/list calls). Produce a concise findings report.",
  "context": "The user asked to 'review my RDS instances and Aurora clusters for best practices compliance and backup configuration'. This is a configuration audit, not a root-cause investigation. Start with the agent space's home account 123456789012 in us-east-1, then use list_associations to find other associated AWS accounts and check them as well. Check us-east-1 first and also any other regions where RDS resources exist (probe commonly used regions, e.g. us-east-2, us-west-2, eu-west-1, and any regions evident from associations/topology). Use jmespath filters to keep outputs small.",
  "resources": ["RDS DB instances (describe_db_instances)", "Aurora/Multi-AZ DB clusters (describe_db_clusters)", "DB cluster/instance snapshots (describe_db_snapshots, describe_db_cluster_snapshots)", "AWS Backup (list_backup_plans, list_protected_resources) if available", "DB parameter groups / event subscriptions"],
  "timeframe": "Current state; for snapshots look at recent automated/manual snapshots (last ~30 days)",
  "criteria": "Backup: BackupRetentionPeriod (flag 0 = disabled, and <7 days), preferred backup window, existence/recency of automated snapshots, manual snapshot hygiene, copy tags to snapshots, cross-region snapshot/backup replication, PITR (LatestRestorableTime), DeletionProtection, AWS Backup coverage, Aurora Backtrack where applicable. Best practices: MultiAZ (instances) / multiple instances across AZs (Aurora clusters), StorageEncrypted + KMS key, PubliclyAccessible, IAM database authentication, AutoMinorVersionUpgrade, engine version/extended support or deprecated versions, Performance Insights enabled, Enhanced Monitoring, CloudWatch log exports, storage autoscaling (MaxAllocatedStorage), gp2 vs gp3, CA certificate expiry/rotation, parameter-group defaults, event subscriptions, tags, SSL enforcement (rds.force_ssl) where checkable, Secrets Manager managed master password, instance class generation (e.g. old previous-gen classes). Return: (1) inventory counts per account/region/engine; (2) a table per resource with key backup settings; (3) prioritized findings grouped High/Medium/Low with the specific resource identifiers and the recommended fix; (4) resources that are fully compliant. If no RDS resources are found in an account/region, say so explicitly. Do NOT make any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review RDS and Aurora backup and best-practice configuration"}], "created_at": null}

